{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore\/init(_:)"]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/init(_:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"init","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"initialEntities","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Entity","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"])","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Does "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" record changes — the data is already persisted."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Important","type":"aside","style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"first-load","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" hydration only. Do not use this initializer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to “refresh from disk” mid-session by assigning into a live "},{"code":"EntityStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(e.g. "},{"code":"state.items = EntityStore(fetched)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from a CloudKit re-hydrate action)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"In-memory state may hold unflushed writes or live UI bindings; wholesale"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"replacement silently drops them and surfaces as lost keystrokes. Use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/merge(from:shouldReplace:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for that path — it records no changes and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lets you decide per-ID which side wins. Under "},{"code":"NSPersistentCloudKitContainer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the gotcha is especially sharp: "},{"code":".NSPersistentStoreRemoteChange","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" fires for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"local saves too, so a naïve “refresh on remote change” observer feeds the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app its own writes."}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Entities sharing an ID are collapsed to the first occurrence. A store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cannot represent duplicates — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"positions"},{"type":"text","text":" holds one index per ID — and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"admitting them corrupts the index: the map would keep only the last"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index while the array kept every copy, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"type":"text","text":" over-reports and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"later delete orphans the earlier copy with no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"positions"},{"type":"text","text":" entry at all,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"leaving a row that is visible in "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/values","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" but invisible to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/contains(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and the subscript. Persisted rows can legitimately"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"share an ID (CloudKit forbids unique constraints), so this initializer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has to be total rather than trusting its input."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"init","externalID":"s:6Swidux11EntityStoreVyACyxGSayxGcfc","roleHeading":"Initializer","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"([","kind":"text"},{"text":"Entity","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"])","kind":"text"}],"title":"init(_:)"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a store pre-populated from an array (e.g. first-load hydration at app launch)."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"title":"EntityStore","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore/merge(from:shouldReplace:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/merge(from:shouldReplace:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore\/merge(from:shouldreplace:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"merge"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"from"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux11EntityStoreV","text":"EntityStore"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"text":"Entity","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text